# .publication-denylist — D8 choice (a): publication-safe pattern notation.
# Per-repo D8 ruling recorded: https://github.com/caty-ai/alpha-nightshift/issues/46
# Format: NAME<TAB>REGEX (Python re, IGNORECASE). One rule per line.
# Patterns are written generically so this committed file exposes no protected literal.
# Scope: repo-specific protected literals only — generic secret shapes (tokens,
# private-key blocks) are gitleaks' job (PR-range caller + full-history sweep),
# and duplicating them here would flag the guard tests' deliberate fixtures.
HOME_ABS_PATH	/Users/[a-z0-9_-]+/
# Personal-account REPOSITORY references (slug/...), not the account name on its
# own: the risk-reviewer roster (.github/risk-reviewers.txt) must name the owner's
# GitHub ID by contract, so a rule forbidding every mention of it can never pass.
# What the seat review actually found was an owner/repo literal the personal-URL
# check cannot see — that is what this rule catches. See issue #50.
PERSONAL_REPO_REF	(?<![A-Za-z0-9-])shojikumaru/
FAMILY_VAULT_PATH	SharedHub/famil[y][-_]vault
ALPHA_WIKI_PATH	claude-workspace/alph[a][-_]wiki
TAILSCALE_CGNAT_IP	\b100\.(6[4-9]|[7-9][0-9]|1[01][0-9]|12[0-7])\.[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}\b
HANDOFF_DIR	_handoff[s]/
